THOUGHT: NullAway now reports two issues in EmitterLoader: dereferencing nullable `emitterXml` at line 34 and returning a @Nullable expression from a method with @NonNull return type at line 52. The task requires fixing only the original DEREFERENCE_NULLABLE on `emitterData` (now line 52) without introducing new errors. Since we intentionally allow `load(@Nullable EmitterData)` to return null, we should annotate its return type as `@Nullable` to match behavior and satisfy NullAway. Also, `load(@Nullable URL emitterXml)` currently dereferences `emitterXml` without a null-check; adding a guard that returns null when `emitterXml` is null will fix that error without changing semantics (callers already expect @Nullable). I’ll update the method signatures and add the null-check.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '32s/public static EmitterData load(@Nullable URL emitterXml)/@Nullable
  public static EmitterData load(@Nullable URL emitterXml)/;34s/^/    if (emitterXml == null) {
      return null;
    }
/;50s/public static EmitterData load(@Nullable EmitterData emitterData)/@Nullable
  public static EmitterData load(@Nullable EmitterData emitterData)/' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/graphics/emitters/xml/EmitterLoader.java
```

